// Soong namespace for the m2note device tree.
//
// WHY (FACT, measured 2026-09-16 on this tree): every Android.bp without a
// soong_namespace lands in the root namespace "." (build/soong/android/
// namespace.go:193), soong_build always exports "." to kati (build/soong/cmd/
// soong_build/main.go:106), and every module of an exported namespace gets
// NamespaceExportedToMake = true (namespace.go:204), which is the only thing
// androidmk.go:919 checks before writing the module's install rule into
// installs-<product>.mk.  Soong has no TARGET_DEVICE guard (kati does), so a
// module declared in ONE device tree gets install rules in EVERY product of
// this workspace.  Measured before this file existed: a plain `m nothing`
// for lineage_m5s carried 51 install-rule lines pointing at 27 modules from
// device/meizu/m95 (installs-lineage_m5s.mk), two of which collided with real
// m5s blobs (vendor/lib{,64}/libperfservicenative.so, from the `stem:` of
// libm95shim_perfservice — a name-only grep does not find those).
//
// A namespace is only exported to Make for products that list it in
// PRODUCT_SOONG_NAMESPACES (see device.mk of this tree); for every other
// product the modules below simply do not reach Make.  Modules inside a
// namespace can still depend on root-namespace modules: the root namespace is
// searched last but it IS searched (namespace.go:288-292).
soong_namespace {
}
